{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3","language":"python"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.15","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"competition","sourceId":149921},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":20795968},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":20796617}],"isInternetEnabled":false,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"f13863ba","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# FORGE-X v2: evidence-checked localization study\n\n**Competition:** Gemma 4 Developer Agent. This notebook is the CPU research harness (Phase 1) plus a corrected submission builder. It replaces v1.\n\n## What v2 changes, and why\nV1's numbers exactly on the real repositories (same 40 tasks: BM25 unit acc@1 0.175; GraphRank and \"E1-FORGE-X\" 0.050), then traced the collapse and the other problems below. Every row of the second column was found by running the v1 code.\n\n| # | Problem in v1 | Evidence | v2 fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Gold labels used whole hunk ranges**, which include about 3 context lines per side, so unchanged neighbouring functions counted as gold | mean 6.45 gold units per task in v1 vs median 1 once only changed lines are used | gold from changed lines only, innermost unit, block-aware attribution of pure insertions |\n| 2 | **Unit identity was the bare qualname**, shared across files | 31.9% of units collide in the same repository | unique ids `path::qualname` |\n| 3 | **Call graph linked a call to every unit with the same bare name** (`get`, `update`, `__init__`...) and propagated mass over all nodes | hubs swamp the ranking; GraphRank acc@5 fell from 0.40 to 0.05 | scoped resolution (`self.x`, same file, imports, repo-unique names), hub damping, bonus restricted to neighbours of the top-K seeds |\n| 4 | **Test code was a candidate** although gold patches exclude tests | excluding tests alone lifts acc@5 from 0.21 to 0.31 on all 129 tasks | tests excluded from candidates (applied to every system) |\n| 5 | **Only the first 40 of 129 tasks** were used (26 FastAPI, 8 Requests, 6 Rich) | | all tasks, with per-repository tables |\n| 6 | **Navigation comparison was unfair**: the \"lexical\" policy used the graph-propagated ranking, and `get_code_subgraph` revealed unbounded units | | every action reveals at most k new units; `rank` is the plain ranking read k at a time |\n| 7 | **Submission builder produced an invalid package**: adapter folder with `adapter_config.json` but no weights, `sub_agents` written as `!include` items instead of `config_path`, prompts that tell the agent to call tools that do not exist | | no adapter unless weights exist, official schema, validated before zipping |\n| 8 | The in-notebook LLM loop was a re-implementation of the harness and never ran | Phase 2 skipped (no model path) | removed; run the agent through `swegemma eval` (see `forge_x_experiments.ipynb`) |\n| 9 | Normal-approximation intervals, no multiplicity control | | bootstrap intervals, sign-flip tests, Holm correction, leave-one-repo-out selection |\n\n## Status of the three contributions after the fixes (measured, 129 tasks)\n- **A, evidence-weighted localization (129 tasks, 107 with a gold unit; graph setting chosen leave-one-repository-out):** most of the improvement over v1 comes from fixing the evaluation and the candidate set. Excluding tests lifts unit MRR by +0.053 (Holm p 0.005) and name/path evidence lifts unit acc@5 by +0.103 (Holm p 0.036). Class-header documents and identifier signals show **no detectable effect**. The graph bonus adds +0.065 unit acc@5 (interval above zero, **not significant after Holm**, p 0.37) and +0.017 MRR (interval includes zero). At weight 1.0 it still hurts, which is the v1 failure mode.\n- **B, failure-conditioned repair:** unit-tested on crafted traces only. **Not evaluated, no claim.**\n- **C, budget-aware navigation:** under a fair cost model **no navigation policy beats simply reading the ranking**; the information-gain policy ties it, and the centrality term does not help.\n\nThe numbers in this cell come from the build run; sections 4 to 6 recompute them.","metadata":{}},{"id":"699841a1","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 0. Setup\nPaths are discovered under `/kaggle/input` or taken from `FORGEX_*` environment variables.","metadata":{}},{"id":"4a7a6924","cell_type":"code","source":"import os, sys, json, time, platform, subprocess, zipfile, hashlib, random, re, shutil, pickle\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSEED = int(os.environ.get(\"FORGEX_SEED\", 0))\nrandom.seed(SEED)\nINPUT_ROOT = Path(os.environ.get(\"FORGEX_INPUT_ROOT\", \"/kaggle/input\"))\n\ndef walk_find(pred, root=INPUT_ROOT, maxdepth=5):\n    hits = []\n    if not root.exists():\n        return hits\n    base = len(root.parts)\n    for dp, dns, fns in os.walk(root):\n        if len(Path(dp).parts) - base >= maxdepth:\n            dns[:] = []\n        for n in dns + fns:\n            p = Path(dp) / n\n            if pred(p):\n                hits.append(p)\n    return sorted(hits)\n\nCFG = dict(\n    TASKS=os.environ.get(\"FORGEX_TASKS\"),\n    SNAPSHOTS=os.environ.get(\"FORGEX_SNAPS\"),\n    ID_FILE=os.environ.get(\"FORGEX_IDS\"),\n    LIMIT=int(os.environ[\"FORGEX_LIMIT\"]) if os.environ.get(\"FORGEX_LIMIT\") else None,   # None = all tasks\n    FIELD_MAP={},\n    ALLOW_UNVERIFIED=False,\n    MODEL_ID=\"gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct\",\n    # localization study\n    RUN_TFIDF=False,                 # TF-IDF added nothing in the build run; set True to re-test\n    GRAPH_BETAS=[0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.5, 1.0],\n    GRAPH_KS=[5, 10, 20],\n    NAV_BUDGET=12, NAV_K=5, NAV_SEEDS=[0, 1, 2],\n    # submission budgets (set after measuring real timings with the swegemma smoke test)\n    SUB_BUDGET=dict(calls=40, minutes=8, turns=100, cmd_timeout=300),\n    OUT=Path(os.environ.get(\"FORGEX_OUT\", \"/kaggle/working/forgex_results\")),\n    SUBMISSION_DIR=Path(os.environ.get(\"FORGEX_SUBMISSION\", \"/kaggle/working/forgex_submission\")),\n)\nCFG[\"OUT\"].mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nprint(\"python\", platform.python_version(), \"| out:\", CFG[\"OUT\"])","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-17T01:40:06.742233Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-17T01:40:06.743914Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-17T01:40:06.781288Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-17T01:40:06.74387Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-17T01:40:06.780792Z"},"trusted":true},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"python 3.13.15 | out: /kaggle/working/forgex_results\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":1},{"id":"272f81a7","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Load tasks\nThe tolerant loader from v1 is unchanged (it resolves several snapshot layouts and flags unverifiable checkouts).","metadata":{}},{"id":"26a5a754","cell_type":"code","source":"# --- Tolerant task loader (SWE-bench-style repos + several snapshot layouts). ---\n_HOT = Path('/tmp/forgex_hot'); _HOT.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n(_HOT / 'forgex_data.py').write_text(r'''\"\"\"data.py - tolerant task loader (jsonl / json) with snapshot resolution.\n\nSupports SWE-bench-style rows (instance_id, repo, base_commit, problem_statement, patch) and\nseveral snapshot layouts under `snapshots_root`:\n\n  per-instance   <snap>/<instance_id>/            (dir)  or  <snap>/<instance_id>.tar.gz|.tgz|.tar|.zip\n                 <snap>/<instance_id>/repo/\n                 <snap>/<repo_key>/<instance_id>/\n  git@commit     <snap>/<repo_key>/  is a git clone (or bare mirror) -> `git archive <base_commit>`\n  per-commit     <snap>/<repo_key>/<base_commit>/  (full or 7/12-char prefix)\n  per-repo       <snap>/<repo_key>/  plain checkout, commit NOT verifiable  (flagged!)\n  fuzzy          any dir/archive (depth<=3) whose normalized name equals/contains the instance id\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json, os, re, shutil, subprocess, tarfile, zipfile\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\nFIELD_CANDIDATES = {\n    \"instance_id\": [\"instance_id\", \"id\", \"task_id\"],\n    \"issue\": [\"problem_statement\", \"issue\", \"issue_text\", \"issue_body\", \"text\", \"description\", \"prompt\"],\n    \"patch\": [\"patch\", \"gold_patch\", \"fix_patch\", \"solution_patch\", \"golden_patch\"],\n    \"repo\": [\"repo_path\", \"repo_dir\", \"snapshot\", \"snapshot_path\", \"repo_root\", \"path\", \"workdir\"],\n    \"repo_id\": [\"repo\", \"repository\", \"repo_name\", \"repo_slug\"],\n    \"commit\": [\"base_commit\", \"commit\", \"base_sha\", \"sha\"],\n}\nARCHIVE_SUFFIXES = (\".tar.gz\", \".tgz\", \".tar\", \".zip\")\n\n\ndef _read_rows(p: Path) -> List[dict]:\n    txt = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    if p.suffix == \".json\":\n        d = json.loads(txt)\n        return d if isinstance(d, list) else d.get(\"tasks\", d.get(\"instances\", []))\n    return [json.loads(l) for l in txt.splitlines() if l.strip()]\n\n\ndef _pick(row: dict, key: str, field_map: Dict[str, str]):\n    if key in field_map:\n        return row.get(field_map[key])\n    for c in FIELD_CANDIDATES[key]:\n        if row.get(c) not in (None, \"\"):\n            return row[c]\n    return None\n\n\ndef _norm(s: str) -> str:\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \"\", s.lower())\n\n\ndef _has_py(d: Path, limit: int = 4000) -> bool:\n    n = 0\n    for _, _, fns in os.walk(d):\n        if any(f.endswith(\".py\") for f in fns):\n            return True\n        n += 1\n        if n > limit:\n            break\n    return False\n\n\ndef _git_dir(p: Path) -> Optional[Path]:\n    if (p / \".git\").exists():\n        return p / \".git\" if (p / \".git\").is_dir() else None\n    if (p / \"HEAD\").is_file() and (p / \"objects\").is_dir():\n        return p\n    return None\n\n\ndef _git_archive(cand: Path, commit: str, out: Path) -> bool:\n    gd = _git_dir(cand)\n    if gd is None or not commit:\n        return False\n    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    tmp = out.parent / f\".{out.name}.tar\"\n    r = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-c\", \"safe.directory=*\", \"--git-dir\", str(gd), \"archive\", \"--format=tar\",\n                        \"-o\", str(tmp), commit], capture_output=True)\n    if r.returncode != 0:\n        shutil.rmtree(out, ignore_errors=True)\n        return False\n    with tarfile.open(tmp) as tf:\n        _safe_extract(tf, out)\n    tmp.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n    return _has_py(out)\n\n\ndef _safe_extract(tf: tarfile.TarFile, out: Path) -> None:\n    try:\n        tf.extractall(out, filter=\"data\")\n    except TypeError:\n        tf.extractall(out)\n\n\ndef _unpack(p: Path, work: Path, tag: str) -> Optional[Path]:\n    out = work / tag\n    if not out.exists():\n        out.mkdir(parents=True)\n        try:\n            if p.name.endswith(\".zip\"):\n                zipfile.ZipFile(p).extractall(out)\n            else:\n                with tarfile.open(p) as tf:\n                    _safe_extract(tf, out)\n        except Exception:\n            shutil.rmtree(out, ignore_errors=True)\n            return None\n    return _descend(out)\n\n\ndef _descend(d: Path) -> Path:\n    subs = [x for x in d.iterdir() if not x.name.startswith(\".\")]\n    if len(subs) == 1 and subs[0].is_dir():\n        return subs[0]\n    return d\n\n\ndef _repo_keys(repo_id: Optional[str], iid: str) -> List[str]:\n    keys: List[str] = []\n    if repo_id:\n        owner, _, name = repo_id.rpartition(\"/\")\n        keys += [repo_id, repo_id.replace(\"/\", \"__\"), repo_id.replace(\"/\", \"_\"), repo_id.replace(\"/\", \"-\"), name]\n        if owner:\n            keys.append(owner)\n    if \"_\" in iid:\n        keys.append(iid.rsplit(\"_\", 1)[0])\n    return list(dict.fromkeys(k for k in keys if k))\n\n\ndef _scan_index(snap: Path, maxdepth: int = 3, cap: int = 5000) -> List[Path]:\n    out, base = [], len(snap.parts)\n    for dp, dns, fns in os.walk(snap):\n        depth = len(Path(dp).parts) - base\n        dns[:] = [d for d in dns if d != \".git\"] if depth < maxdepth else []\n        for n in dns + [f for f in fns if f.endswith(ARCHIVE_SUFFIXES)]:\n            out.append(Path(dp) / n)\n        if len(out) > cap:\n            break\n    return out\n\n\ndef resolve_snapshot(snap, tasks_dir, work, iid, repo_path, repo_id, commit, _index_cache):\n    if repo_path:\n        rp = Path(str(repo_path))\n        for c in [rp, tasks_dir / rp] + ([snap / rp] if snap else []):\n            if c.is_dir():\n                return _descend(c) if not _has_py(c) else c, \"per-instance\"\n            if c.is_file() and c.name.endswith(ARCHIVE_SUFFIXES):\n                d = _unpack(c, work, iid)\n                if d:\n                    return d, \"per-instance\"\n    roots = ([snap] if snap else []) + [tasks_dir / \"snapshots\"]\n    keys = _repo_keys(repo_id, iid)\n    for root in roots:\n        if not root.exists():\n            continue\n        per = [root / iid, root / iid / \"repo\"] + [root / f\"{iid}{s}\" for s in ARCHIVE_SUFFIXES] + \\\n              [root / k / iid for k in keys]\n        for c in per:\n            if c.is_dir() and _has_py(c):\n                return c, \"per-instance\"\n            if c.is_file() and c.name.endswith(ARCHIVE_SUFFIXES):\n                d = _unpack(c, work, iid)\n                if d and _has_py(d):\n                    return d, \"per-instance\"\n        for k in keys:\n            for c in (root / k, root / k / \"repo\", root / k.replace(\"__\", \"/\")):\n                if not c.is_dir():\n                    continue\n                if commit and _git_dir(c):\n                    out = work / f\"{iid}_git\"\n                    if (out.exists() and _has_py(out)) or _git_archive(c, commit, out):\n                        return out, \"git@base_commit\"\n                if commit:\n                    for sub in (commit, commit[:12], commit[:7]):\n                        if (c / sub).is_dir() and _has_py(c / sub):\n                            return c / sub, \"per-commit\"\n                if _has_py(c):\n                    return c, \"per-repo (commit NOT verified)\"\n        idx = _index_cache.setdefault(str(root), _scan_index(root))\n        ni = _norm(iid)\n        for p in idx:\n            nm = _norm(p.name.split(\".\")[0] if p.is_file() else p.name)\n            if nm == ni or (len(ni) >= 6 and ni in nm):\n                if p.is_dir() and _has_py(p):\n                    return p, \"fuzzy\"\n                if p.is_file():\n                    d = _unpack(p, work, iid)\n                    if d and _has_py(d):\n                        return d, \"fuzzy\"\n    return None, \"unresolved\"\n\n\ndef describe_layout(snap, max_entries: int = 40, depth: int = 2) -> str:\n    if not snap or not Path(snap).exists():\n        return f\"(snapshots path does not exist: {snap})\"\n    snap, lines, base = Path(snap), [], len(Path(snap).parts)\n    for dp, dns, fns in os.walk(snap):\n        d = len(Path(dp).parts) - base\n        dns[:] = sorted(x for x in dns if x != \".git\") if d < depth else []\n        for n in sorted(dns) + sorted(fns)[:5]:\n            lines.append(\"  \" * (d + 1) + n + (\"/\" if n in dns else \"\"))\n        if len(lines) >= max_entries:\n            lines.append(\"  ... (truncated)\")\n            break\n    return f\"{snap}\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(lines[:max_entries + 1])\n\n\ndef load_ids(path):\n    if not path or not Path(path).exists():\n        return None\n    return [l.strip() for l in Path(path).read_text().splitlines() if l.strip() and not l.startswith(\"#\")]\n\n\ndef load_tasks(tasks_path, snapshots_root=None, ids=None, limit=None, field_map=None,\n               work_dir=\"/tmp/forgex_snapshots\"):\n    tasks_path, work = Path(tasks_path), Path(work_dir)\n    work.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    field_map = field_map or {}\n    snap = Path(snapshots_root) if snapshots_root else None\n    rows = _read_rows(tasks_path)\n    if ids:\n        order = {i: n for n, i in enumerate(ids)}\n        rows = sorted((r for r in rows if str(_pick(r, \"instance_id\", field_map)) in order),\n                      key=lambda r: order[str(_pick(r, \"instance_id\", field_map))])\n    tasks, cache = [], {}\n    report = {\"rows\": len(rows), \"no_issue\": 0, \"no_patch\": 0, \"no_repo\": 0, \"kinds\": Counter(),\n              \"columns\": sorted(rows[0]) if rows else []}\n    for r in rows:\n        iid = str(_pick(r, \"instance_id\", field_map))\n        issue, patch = _pick(r, \"issue\", field_map), _pick(r, \"patch\", field_map)\n        repo_path = _pick(r, \"repo\", field_map)\n        repo_id, commit = _pick(r, \"repo_id\", field_map), _pick(r, \"commit\", field_map)\n        root, kind = resolve_snapshot(snap, tasks_path.parent, work, iid, repo_path, repo_id or repo_path, commit, cache)\n        report[\"no_issue\"] += issue is None\n        report[\"no_patch\"] += patch is None\n        report[\"no_repo\"] += root is None\n        report[\"kinds\"][kind] += 1\n        tasks.append({\"instance_id\": iid, \"issue\": issue or \"\", \"patch\": patch, \"repo_root\": root,\n                      \"snapshot_kind\": kind, \"base_commit\": commit, \"repo_id\": repo_id, \"raw\": r})\n        if limit and len(tasks) >= limit:\n            break\n    report[\"kinds\"] = dict(report[\"kinds\"])\n    if report[\"no_repo\"]:\n        t = next((t for t in tasks if t[\"repo_root\"] is None), None)\n        report[\"unresolved_example\"] = {k: t[k] for k in (\"instance_id\", \"repo_id\", \"base_commit\")} if t else None\n        report[\"layout\"] = describe_layout(snap)\n    return tasks, report\n''')\nsys.path.insert(0, str(_HOT))\nimport importlib, forgex_data\nimportlib.reload(forgex_data)\nfrom forgex_data import load_tasks, load_ids\nprint('task loader active')","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-17T01:40:06.873382Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-17T01:40:06.873648Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-17T01:40:06.890603Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-17T01:40:06.873626Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-17T01:40:06.889883Z"},"trusted":true},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"task loader active\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":2},{"id":"0633f7df","cell_type":"code","source":"tp = CFG[\"TASKS\"]\nif not tp:\n    cands = walk_find(lambda p: p.is_file() and p.suffix in (\".jsonl\", \".json\") and \"task\" in p.name.lower())\n    assert cands, \"No tasks file found: set FORGEX_TASKS.\"\n    tp = str(cands[0])\nsnap = CFG[\"SNAPSHOTS\"]\nif not snap:\n    s = walk_find(lambda p: p.is_dir() and p.name in (\"snapshots\", \"repos\"))\n    snap = str(s[0]) if s else None\nids = load_ids(CFG[\"ID_FILE\"])\ntasks, rep = load_tasks(tp, snap, ids=ids, limit=CFG[\"LIMIT\"], field_map=CFG[\"FIELD_MAP\"])\nprint(\"tasks file :\", tp, \"\\nsnapshots  :\", snap, \"\\ncolumns    :\", rep[\"columns\"])\nprint({k: v for k, v in rep.items() if k not in (\"columns\", \"layout\", \"unresolved_example\")})\nassert tasks, \"No tasks loaded.\"\nusable = [t for t in tasks if t[\"repo_root\"] is not None]\nassert usable, \"No repo snapshots resolved.\"\nunverified = [t for t in usable if \"NOT verified\" in t[\"snapshot_kind\"]]\nif unverified and not CFG[\"ALLOW_UNVERIFIED\"]:\n    print(f\"WARNING: {len(unverified)} tasks use unverified per-repo checkouts; excluded (CFG['ALLOW_UNVERIFIED']=True keeps them).\")\n    usable = [t for t in usable if t not in unverified]\ntasks = [t for t in usable if t[\"patch\"]]\nfrom collections import Counter\nprint(f\"{len(tasks)} tasks with snapshot and gold patch | repositories: {dict(Counter(t['repo_id'] for t in tasks))}\")","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-17T01:40:06.891721Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-17T01:40:06.892018Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-17T01:43:49.750515Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-17T01:40:06.891989Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-17T01:43:49.74987Z"},"trusted":true},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"tasks file : /kaggle/input/competitions/gemma-4-developer-agent/tasks.jsonl \nsnapshots  : /kaggle/input/competitions/gemma-4-developer-agent/snapshots \ncolumns    : ['base_commit', 'created_at', 'hints_text', 'instance_id', 'patch', 'problem_statement', 'repo', 'test_patch']\n{'rows': 129, 'no_issue': 0, 'no_patch': 0, 'no_repo': 0, 'kinds': {'per-instance': 129}}\n129 tasks with snapshot and gold patch | repositories: {'fastapi/fastapi': 67, 'psf/requests': 13, 'Textualize/rich': 48, 'encode/httpx': 1}\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"id":"49b881d6","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. FORGE-X core library v2 and self-tests\nThe package is written to `/tmp/forgex_pkg/forgex` so it is importable and self-contained. The self-tests run real assertions, including regression tests for the labelling bugs found in v1.","metadata":{}},{"id":"ea77c2ad","cell_type":"code","source":"from pathlib import Path\nPKG = Path('/tmp/forgex_pkg/forgex')\nPKG.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nMODULES = {}\n\nMODULES['__init__.py'] = r'''\"\"\"FORGE-X core v2.\"\"\"\nfrom .ast_index import index_repo, Unit, FileInfo, is_test_path\nfrom .localize import EvidenceLocalizer, issue_identifiers\nfrom .gold import parse_changes, gold_units, gold_files\nfrom .metrics import rank_metrics, mean_rows, boot_ci, signflip_p, holm, paired\nfrom . import failure, budget, env\nfrom .env import NavEnv, run_nav, POLICIES\n\n__all__ = [\"index_repo\", \"Unit\", \"FileInfo\", \"is_test_path\", \"EvidenceLocalizer\", \"issue_identifiers\",\n           \"parse_changes\", \"gold_units\", \"gold_files\", \"rank_metrics\", \"mean_rows\", \"boot_ci\", \"signflip_p\",\n           \"holm\", \"paired\", \"failure\", \"budget\", \"env\", \"NavEnv\", \"run_nav\", \"POLICIES\"]\n'''\n\nMODULES['tokens.py'] = r'''\"\"\"Shared identifier tokenizer (camelCase / snake_case aware).\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport re\n\n_WORD = re.compile(r\"[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\")\n\ndef tokenize(s: str):\n    out = []\n    for m in _WORD.finditer(s or \"\"):\n        w = re.sub(r\"([a-z0-9])([A-Z])\", r\"\\1 \\2\", m.group(0))\n        for t in w.replace(\"_\", \" \").split():\n            t = t.lower()\n            if t:\n                out.append(t)\n    return out\n'''\n\nMODULES['ast_index.py'] = r'''\"\"\"AST index v2: unique unit ids (path::qualname), per-file import maps, scoped call records.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport ast\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSKIP_DIRS = {\".git\", \".hg\", \".svn\", \"node_modules\", \"site-packages\", \".venv\", \"venv\", \"env\",\n             \"__pycache__\", \"build\", \"dist\", \".tox\", \".mypy_cache\", \".pytest_cache\", \".eggs\"}\nTEST_DIRS = {\"tests\", \"test\", \"testing\"}\n\n\ndef is_test_path(p: str) -> bool:\n    parts = p.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\").lower().split(\"/\")\n    name = parts[-1]\n    return (any(x in TEST_DIRS for x in parts[:-1]) or name.startswith(\"test_\")\n            or name.endswith(\"_test.py\") or name == \"conftest.py\")\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Unit:\n    uid: str\n    name: str\n    qualname: str\n    kind: str                # \"function\" | \"class\"\n    path: str\n    start: int\n    end: int\n    indent: int              # column of the def/class keyword\n    text: str\n    doc: str = \"\"\n    calls: list = field(default_factory=list)    # [(mode, name)] mode: name | self | attr\n    bases: list = field(default_factory=list)\n    parent: str | None = None                    # uid of the enclosing unit\n    is_test: bool = False\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass FileInfo:\n    path: str\n    module: str\n    is_pkg: bool\n    imports: dict = field(default_factory=dict)  # local name -> (dotted module, symbol | None)\n    n_lines: int = 0\n\n\ndef _calls(node):\n    out = set()\n    for c in ast.walk(node):\n        if isinstance(c, ast.Call):\n            f = c.func\n            if isinstance(f, ast.Name):\n                out.add((\"name\", f.id))\n            elif isinstance(f, ast.Attribute):\n                if isinstance(f.value, ast.Name) and f.value.id in (\"self\", \"cls\"):\n                    out.add((\"self\", f.attr))\n                else:\n                    out.add((\"attr\", f.attr))\n    return sorted(out)\n\n\ndef _base_name(b):\n    if isinstance(b, ast.Name):\n        return b.id\n    if isinstance(b, ast.Attribute):\n        return b.attr\n    return None\n\n\nclass _Visitor(ast.NodeVisitor):\n    def __init__(self, path, lines, test):\n        self.path, self.lines, self.test = path, lines, test\n        self.units, self.stack = [], []          # stack of (name, uid)\n\n    def _text(self, node):\n        return \"\\n\".join(self.lines[node.lineno - 1:getattr(node, \"end_lineno\", node.lineno)])\n\n    def _add(self, node, kind, calls, bases):\n        q = \".\".join([n for n, _ in self.stack] + [node.name])\n        uid = f\"{self.path}::{q}\"\n        doc = ast.get_docstring(node) or \"\"\n        start = min([node.lineno] + [d.lineno for d in getattr(node, \"decorator_list\", [])])\n        self.units.append(Unit(uid, node.name, q, kind, self.path, start,\n                               getattr(node, \"end_lineno\", node.lineno), node.col_offset, self._text(node),\n                               doc, calls, bases, self.stack[-1][1] if self.stack else None, self.test))\n        self.stack.append((node.name, uid))\n        self.generic_visit(node)\n        self.stack.pop()\n\n    def visit_FunctionDef(self, node):\n        self._add(node, \"function\", _calls(node), [])\n\n    visit_AsyncFunctionDef = visit_FunctionDef\n\n    def visit_ClassDef(self, node):\n        self._add(node, \"class\", [], [b for b in (_base_name(x) for x in node.bases) if b])\n\n\ndef _module_name(rel):\n    parts = rel[:-3].split(\"/\")\n    is_pkg = parts[-1] == \"__init__\"\n    if is_pkg:\n        parts = parts[:-1]\n    return \".\".join(parts), is_pkg\n\n\ndef _imports(tree, module, is_pkg):\n    imps = {}\n    pkg = module if is_pkg else module.rpartition(\".\")[0]\n    for n in ast.walk(tree):\n        if isinstance(n, ast.Import):\n            for a in n.names:\n                imps[a.asname or a.name.split(\".\")[0]] = (a.name if a.asname else a.name.split(\".\")[0], None)\n        elif isinstance(n, ast.ImportFrom):\n            base = n.module or \"\"\n            if n.level:\n                up = pkg.split(\".\") if pkg else []\n                up = up[:len(up) - (n.level - 1)] if n.level > 1 else up\n                base = \".\".join([x for x in up + ([n.module] if n.module else []) if x])\n            for a in n.names:\n                if a.name != \"*\":\n                    imps[a.asname or a.name] = (base, a.name)\n    return imps\n\n\ndef index_repo(root):\n    root = Path(root)\n    units, files = [], {}\n    for p in sorted(root.rglob(\"*.py\")):\n        rel = p.relative_to(root).as_posix()\n        if set(rel.split(\"/\")) & SKIP_DIRS:\n            continue\n        try:\n            src = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\")\n            tree = ast.parse(src)\n        except Exception:\n            continue\n        mod, is_pkg = _module_name(rel)\n        files[rel] = FileInfo(rel, mod, is_pkg, _imports(tree, mod, is_pkg), src.count(\"\\n\") + 1)\n        v = _Visitor(rel, src.splitlines(), is_test_path(rel))\n        v.visit(tree)\n        units.extend(v.units)\n    return units, files\n'''\n\nMODULES['bm25.py'] = r'''\"\"\"Minimal BM25 over code units.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport math\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom .tokens import tokenize\n\nclass BM25:\n    def __init__(self, docs, k1=1.5, b=0.75):\n        self.k1, self.b = k1, b\n        self.docs = [tokenize(d) for d in docs]\n        self.N = len(self.docs)\n        self.avgdl = (sum(len(d) for d in self.docs) / self.N) if self.N else 0.0\n        self.tf = [Counter(d) for d in self.docs]\n        df = Counter()\n        for d in self.docs:\n            df.update(set(d))\n        self.idf = {w: math.log(1 + (self.N - c + 0.5) / (c + 0.5)) for w, c in df.items()}\n\n    def scores(self, query):\n        qt = tokenize(query)\n        out = []\n        for i, cf in enumerate(self.tf):\n            dl = len(self.docs[i]) or 1\n            s = 0.0\n            for w in qt:\n                f = cf.get(w, 0)\n                if not f:\n                    continue\n                idf = self.idf.get(w, 0.0)\n                s += idf * f * (self.k1 + 1) / (f + self.k1 * (1 - self.b + self.b * dl / self.avgdl))\n            out.append(s)\n        return out\n'''\n\nMODULES['similarity.py'] = r'''\"\"\"TF-IDF cosine similarity, plus an explicit hashed-embedding fallback.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport math\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom .tokens import tokenize\n\nclass TfidfCosine:\n    def __init__(self, docs):\n        self.docs = [tokenize(d) for d in docs]\n        df = Counter()\n        for d in self.docs:\n            df.update(set(d))\n        n = len(self.docs) or 1\n        self.idf = {w: math.log((1 + n) / (1 + c)) + 1 for w, c in df.items()}\n        self.default_idf = math.log(1 + n) + 1\n        self.vec = [self._v(d) for d in self.docs]\n\n    def _v(self, toks):\n        tf = Counter(toks)\n        v = {w: tf[w] * self.idf.get(w, self.default_idf) for w in tf}\n        norm = math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in v.values())) or 1.0\n        return {w: x / norm for w, x in v.items()}\n\n    def scores(self, query):\n        qv = self._v(tokenize(query))\n        out = []\n        for v in self.vec:\n            a, b = (v, qv) if len(v) < len(qv) else (qv, v)\n            out.append(sum(x * b.get(w, 0.0) for w, x in a.items()))\n        return out\n\ndef hash_embed(text, dim=256):\n    \"\"\"Deterministic hashed bag-of-identifiers embedding. NOT a learned embedding; used only\n    when the harness's 256-d embeddings are unavailable, and always labelled as such.\"\"\"\n    v = [0.0] * dim\n    for t in tokenize(text):\n        v[hash(t) % dim] += 1.0\n    norm = math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in v)) or 1.0\n    return [x / norm for x in v]\n\ndef cosine(a, b):\n    return sum(x * y for x, y in zip(a, b))\n'''\n\nMODULES['graphprop.py'] = r'''\"\"\"Scoped call-graph construction (v2) and seed-restricted evidence propagation.\n\nv1 linked a call to EVERY unit sharing its bare name (get, update, __init__ ...), merged units with equal\nqualnames across files, and diffused mass over all nodes. That makes hubs and wrecks the ranking. Here an edge is\ncreated only when the target can be resolved with some confidence:\n  self.x()   -> method x of the enclosing class (or its resolvable bases)\n  x()        -> x in the same file, else the symbol imported under that name, else a repo-unique x\n  obj.x()    -> only if exactly one non-test unit is called x repo-wide\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport math\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\n\ndef _enclosing_class(u, by_uid):\n    p = u.parent\n    while p:\n        pu = by_uid.get(p)\n        if pu is None:\n            return None\n        if pu.kind == \"class\":\n            return pu\n        p = pu.parent\n    return None\n\n\ndef build_edges(units, files):\n    \"\"\"Return (adj, stats). adj: uid -> set(uid), undirected, test units excluded.\"\"\"\n    src = [u for u in units if not u.is_test]\n    by_uid = {u.uid: u for u in src}\n    by_file = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(list))      # path -> name -> [uid] (any depth)\n    methods = defaultdict(dict)                           # class uid -> {name: uid}\n    glob = defaultdict(list)                              # name -> [uid]\n    classes = defaultdict(list)                           # class name -> [uid]\n    for u in src:\n        by_file[u.path][u.name].append(u.uid)\n        if not u.name.startswith(\"__\"):\n            glob[u.name].append(u.uid)\n        if u.parent and by_uid.get(u.parent) is not None and by_uid[u.parent].kind == \"class\":\n            methods[u.parent][u.name] = u.uid\n        if u.kind == \"class\":\n            classes[u.name].append(u.uid)\n    mod_to_path = {}\n    for path, fi in files.items():\n        mod_to_path.setdefault(fi.module, path)\n        parts = fi.module.split(\".\")\n        if len(parts) > 1 and parts[0] in (\"src\", \"lib\"):\n            mod_to_path.setdefault(\".\".join(parts[1:]), path)\n\n    def method_lookup(cls, name, depth=0):\n        if name in methods.get(cls.uid, {}):\n            return methods[cls.uid][name]\n        if depth >= 3:\n            return None\n        for b in cls.bases:\n            cands = [c for c in classes.get(b, []) if by_uid[c].path == cls.path] or \\\n                    (classes.get(b, []) if len(classes.get(b, [])) == 1 else [])\n            for c in cands:\n                r = method_lookup(by_uid[c], name, depth + 1)\n                if r:\n                    return r\n        return None\n\n    adj, n_resolved, n_calls = defaultdict(set), 0, 0\n    for u in src:\n        fi = files.get(u.path)\n        for mode, name in u.calls:\n            n_calls += 1\n            tgt = None\n            if mode == \"self\":\n                cls = _enclosing_class(u, by_uid)\n                tgt = method_lookup(cls, name) if cls else None\n            elif mode == \"name\":\n                same = by_file[u.path].get(name, [])\n                if len(same) >= 1:\n                    tgt = next((s for s in same if s != u.uid), None)\n                elif fi and name in fi.imports:\n                    mod, sym = fi.imports[name]\n                    p = mod_to_path.get(mod)\n                    cand = by_file[p].get(sym or name, []) if p else []\n                    tgt = cand[0] if len(cand) == 1 else None\n                if tgt is None and len(glob.get(name, [])) == 1:\n                    tgt = glob[name][0]\n            else:\n                if len(glob.get(name, [])) == 1:\n                    tgt = glob[name][0]\n            if tgt and tgt != u.uid:\n                adj[u.uid].add(tgt)\n                adj[tgt].add(u.uid)\n                n_resolved += 1\n    return adj, {\"calls\": n_calls, \"resolved\": n_resolved,\n                 \"max_degree\": max((len(v) for v in adj.values()), default=0)}\n\n\ndef propagate_bonus(base, adj, seeds_k=10, steps=1, hub_cap=25):\n    \"\"\"Bonus for neighbours of the top-K seeds, damped by 1/sqrt(degree). base: dict uid -> score.\"\"\"\n    top = sorted(base, key=base.get, reverse=True)[:seeds_k]\n    bonus = defaultdict(float)\n    frontier = {s: base[s] for s in top if base[s] > 0}\n    for _ in range(max(1, steps)):\n        nxt = defaultdict(float)\n        for n, s in frontier.items():\n            nb = adj.get(n, ())\n            if not nb or len(nb) > hub_cap:\n                continue\n            for m in nb:\n                nxt[m] += s / math.sqrt(len(nb) * max(1, len(adj.get(m, ()))))\n        for m, v in nxt.items():\n            bonus[m] += v\n        frontier = nxt\n    return bonus\n'''\n\nMODULES['gold.py'] = r'''\"\"\"Gold labels from a unified diff (v2). Uses CHANGED lines only (v1 used whole hunk ranges, which include\n~3 context lines on each side, so neighbouring unchanged functions counted as gold).\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport re\n\n_HUNK = re.compile(r\"^@@ -(\\d+)(?:,(\\d+))? \\+(\\d+)(?:,(\\d+))? @@\")\n\n\ndef parse_changes(patch):\n    \"\"\"{path: {\"rem\": set(old line numbers), \"ins\": [(anchor_old_line, min_indent|None)], \"new\": bool}}\"\"\"\n    files, cur, old_ln, block = {}, None, None, []\n\n    def flush():\n        nonlocal block\n        if cur is not None and block:\n            ind = [i for i in block if i is not None]\n            files[cur][\"ins\"].append((old_ln, min(ind) if ind else None))\n        block = []\n\n    for line in (patch or \"\").splitlines():\n        if line.startswith(\"diff --git\"):\n            flush(); cur, old_ln = None, None\n        elif line.startswith(\"--- \") and old_ln is None:\n            continue\n        elif line.startswith(\"+++ \") and old_ln is None:\n            p = line[4:].strip()\n            p = p[2:] if p.startswith(\"b/\") else p\n            cur = None if p == \"/dev/null\" else p\n            if cur:\n                files.setdefault(cur, {\"rem\": set(), \"ins\": [], \"new\": False})\n        elif line.startswith(\"@@\"):\n            flush()\n            m = _HUNK.match(line)\n            if m and cur:\n                old_ln = int(m.group(1))\n                if int(m.group(2) or 1) == 0 and old_ln == 0:\n                    files[cur][\"new\"] = True\n        elif cur is not None and old_ln is not None:\n            if line.startswith(\"+\"):\n                body = line[1:]\n                block.append(len(body) - len(body.lstrip()) if body.strip() else None)\n            elif line.startswith(\"-\"):\n                flush(); files[cur][\"rem\"].add(old_ln); old_ln += 1\n            elif line.startswith(\"\\\\\"):\n                continue\n            else:\n                flush(); old_ln += 1\n    flush()\n    return files\n\n\ndef _innermost(spans, ln):\n    best = None\n    for u in spans:\n        if u.start <= ln <= u.end and (best is None or (u.end - u.start) < (best.end - best.start)):\n            best = u\n    return best\n\n\ndef _ancestors(uid, by_uid):\n    out = []\n    while uid in by_uid:\n        out.append(uid)\n        uid = by_uid[uid].parent\n    return out\n\n\ndef gold_units(units, changes):\n    \"\"\"Set of unit uids touched by the change (innermost unit per changed line / inserted block).\"\"\"\n    by_path, by_uid = {}, {u.uid: u for u in units}\n    for u in units:\n        by_path.setdefault(u.path, []).append(u)\n    out = set()\n    for path, ch in changes.items():\n        spans = by_path.get(path)\n        if not spans or ch[\"new\"]:\n            continue\n        for ln in ch[\"rem\"]:\n            u = _innermost(spans, ln)\n            if u:\n                out.add(u.uid)\n        for anchor, indent in ch[\"ins\"]:\n            if indent is None:\n                continue\n            c1, c2 = _innermost(spans, anchor - 1), _innermost(spans, anchor)\n            if c1 is c2:\n                u = c1 if indent > 0 else None\n            elif c1 is not None and indent > c1.indent:\n                u = c1                                            # block is deeper than c1's def line: body of c1\n            elif c1 is not None and c2 is not None:\n                a2 = set(_ancestors(c2.uid, by_uid))\n                u = next((by_uid[a] for a in _ancestors(c1.uid, by_uid) if a in a2), None)\n            else:\n                u = (c1 or c2) if indent > 0 else None\n            if u:\n                out.add(u.uid)\n    return out\n\n\ndef gold_files(changes):\n    return {p for p in changes if p.endswith(\".py\")}\n'''\n\nMODULES['metrics.py'] = r'''\"\"\"Ranking metrics, bootstrap intervals and paired comparisons.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport random\n\n\ndef rank_metrics(order, gold, ks=(1, 3, 5, 10)):\n    gold = set(gold or [])\n    m = {f\"acc@{k}\": 1.0 if (gold & set(order[:k])) else 0.0 for k in ks}\n    m[\"mrr\"] = 0.0\n    for i, n in enumerate(order, 1):\n        if n in gold:\n            m[\"mrr\"] = 1.0 / i\n            break\n    m[\"recall@5\"] = len(gold & set(order[:5])) / len(gold) if gold else 0.0\n    return m\n\n\ndef mean_rows(rows, keys):\n    out = {}\n    for k in keys:\n        vals = [r[k] for r in rows if k in r]\n        out[k] = sum(vals) / len(vals) if vals else 0.0\n    return out\n\n\ndef boot_ci(vals, n=4000, seed=7):\n    vals = list(vals)\n    if not vals:\n        return (float(\"nan\"), float(\"nan\"))\n    rng, m = random.Random(seed), len(vals)\n    bs = sorted(sum(vals[rng.randrange(m)] for _ in range(m)) / m for _ in range(n))\n    return bs[int(0.025 * n)], bs[int(0.975 * n) - 1]\n\n\ndef signflip_p(d, n=20000, seed=11):\n    d = [x for x in d]\n    if not d:\n        return float(\"nan\")\n    rng, obs = random.Random(seed), abs(sum(d))\n    hits = sum(abs(sum(x if rng.random() < 0.5 else -x for x in d)) >= obs - 1e-12 for _ in range(n))\n    return (hits + 1) / (n + 1)\n\n\ndef holm(pvals):\n    order = sorted(range(len(pvals)), key=lambda i: pvals[i])\n    adj, run = [0.0] * len(pvals), 0.0\n    for rank, i in enumerate(order):\n        run = max(run, (len(pvals) - rank) * pvals[i])\n        adj[i] = min(1.0, run)\n    return adj\n\n\ndef paired(rows_a, rows_b, key):\n    a = {r[\"instance_id\"]: r[key] for r in rows_a if key in r}\n    b = {r[\"instance_id\"]: r[key] for r in rows_b if key in r}\n    ids = sorted(set(a) & set(b))\n    d = [b[i] - a[i] for i in ids]\n    if not d:\n        return None\n    lo, hi = boot_ci(d)\n    return {\"n\": len(d), \"mean_diff\": sum(d) / len(d), \"ci95\": (lo, hi), \"p\": signflip_p(d),\n            \"wins\": sum(x > 0 for x in d), \"losses\": sum(x < 0 for x in d)}\n'''\n\nMODULES['localize.py'] = r'''\"\"\"Contribution A (v2): evidence-weighted localization over unique code units.\n\nEvidence: BM25 over unit documents, exact identifier / path signals taken from the issue, optional TF-IDF\nsimilarity, and a small, seed-restricted graph bonus. Test code is excluded from the candidates (gold patches\nexclude tests). prepare() computes the expensive parts once so knobs can be swept cheaply.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport re\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom .bm25 import BM25\nfrom .similarity import TfidfCosine\nfrom .graphprop import build_edges, propagate_bonus\nfrom .tokens import tokenize\n\n_ID = re.compile(r\"[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\")\n_PATH = re.compile(r\"([\\w/\\.\\-]+\\.py)\")\n\n\ndef _norm(v):\n    hi = max(v) if v else 0.0\n    return [x / hi for x in v] if hi > 0 else [0.0] * len(v)\n\n\ndef issue_identifiers(issue):\n    ids = set()\n    for m in re.finditer(r\"`([^`\\n]+)`\", issue or \"\"):\n        ids.update(_ID.findall(m.group(1)))\n    for t in _ID.findall(issue or \"\"):\n        if (\"_\" in t.strip(\"_\")) or re.search(r\"[a-z][A-Z]\", t):\n            ids.add(t)\n    return {i for i in ids if len(i) > 2}\n\n\nclass EvidenceLocalizer:\n    def __init__(self, units, files, exclude_tests=True, doc_mode=\"v2\"):\n        self.units = [u for u in units if not (exclude_tests and u.is_test)]\n        self.by_uid = {u.uid: u for u in self.units}\n        kids = defaultdict(list)\n        for u in self.units:\n            if u.parent:\n                kids[u.parent].append(u.name)\n\n        def doc(u):\n            if doc_mode == \"v1\" or u.kind != \"class\":\n                return f\"{u.name} {u.qualname} {u.doc} {u.text}\" if doc_mode != \"v1\" else f\"{u.name} {u.qualname} {u.text}\"\n            return f\"{u.name} {u.qualname} {u.doc} \" + \" \".join(kids.get(u.uid, []))   # class: header, not all bodies\n\n        docs = [doc(u) for u in self.units]\n        self.bm25 = BM25(docs)\n        self.name_bm25 = BM25([f\"{u.name} {u.qualname} {u.path}\" for u in self.units])\n        self._tfidf = None\n        self._docs = docs\n        self.adj, self.graph_stats = build_edges(units, files)\n        self.files = files\n\n    def tfidf(self):\n        if self._tfidf is None:\n            self._tfidf = TfidfCosine(self._docs)\n        return self._tfidf\n\n    def neighbors(self, uid):\n        return sorted(self.adj.get(uid, ()))\n\n    def degree(self, uid):\n        return len(self.adj.get(uid, ()))\n\n    def prepare(self, query):\n        ids, paths = issue_identifiers(query), set(_PATH.findall(query or \"\"))\n        sig = []\n        for u in self.units:\n            s = 0.0\n            if u.name in ids:\n                s += 1.0\n            parts = u.qualname.split(\".\")\n            if any(p in ids for p in parts[:-1]):\n                s += 0.5\n            if any(u.path == p or u.path.endswith(\"/\" + p) or u.path.endswith(p) for p in paths):\n                s += 1.0\n            sig.append(s)\n        return {\"lex\": _norm(self.bm25.scores(query)), \"name\": _norm(self.name_bm25.scores(query)),\n                \"sig\": _norm(sig), \"sim\": None, \"query\": query}\n\n    def unit_scores(self, prep, w_lex=1.0, w_name=0.3, w_sig=0.5, w_sim=0.0, beta=0.0, K=10, steps=1):\n        if w_sim and prep[\"sim\"] is None:\n            prep[\"sim\"] = _norm(self.tfidf().scores(prep[\"query\"]))\n        sim = prep[\"sim\"] or [0.0] * len(self.units)\n        base = {u.uid: w_lex * prep[\"lex\"][i] + w_name * prep[\"name\"][i] + w_sig * prep[\"sig\"][i] + w_sim * sim[i]\n                for i, u in enumerate(self.units)}\n        if beta > 0:\n            bonus = propagate_bonus(base, self.adj, seeds_k=K, steps=steps)\n            hi = max(bonus.values(), default=0.0)\n            if hi > 0:\n                top = max(base.values()) or 1.0\n                for k, v in bonus.items():\n                    if k in base:\n                        base[k] += beta * top * (v / hi)\n        return base\n\n    def rank_units(self, prep, **kw):\n        if isinstance(prep, str):\n            prep = self.prepare(prep)\n        sc = self.unit_scores(prep, **kw)\n        return [k for k, _ in sorted(sc.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1], kv[0]))]\n\n    def rank_files(self, prep, file_mix=0.0, **kw):\n        if isinstance(prep, str):\n            prep = self.prepare(prep)\n        sc = self.unit_scores(prep, **kw)\n        per = defaultdict(list)\n        for uid, s in sc.items():\n            per[self.by_uid[uid].path].append(s)\n        fs = {p: max(v) + file_mix * sum(sorted(v, reverse=True)[1:3]) for p, v in per.items()}\n        return [p for p, _ in sorted(fs.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1], kv[0]))]\n'''\n\nMODULES['failure.py'] = r'''\"\"\"Contribution B: failure-conditioned repair.\n\nClassify why a repair attempt failed and pick a different next action instead of\nrepeating the same strategy.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport re\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n\nFAILURE_CLASSES = (\"localization_error\", \"implementation_error\", \"regression\",\n                   \"incomplete_verification\", \"unknown\")\n\nNEXT_ACTION = {\n    \"localization_error\": {\"tool\": \"get_code_neighbors\",\n                           \"why\": \"expand the graph around the failing test's callers\"},\n    \"implementation_error\": {\"tool\": \"edit_file\",\n                             \"why\": \"re-read the edited unit and change the logic again\"},\n    \"regression\": {\"tool\": \"run_command\",\n                   \"why\": \"inspect and revert the change that broke passing tests\"},\n    \"incomplete_verification\": {\"tool\": \"run_command\",\n                                \"why\": \"run the failing tests to observe real behaviour\"},\n    \"unknown\": {\"tool\": \"get_code_subgraph\",\n                \"why\": \"gather more context before committing to a strategy\"},\n}\n\n_FAIL_LINE = re.compile(r\"(?:FAILED|ERROR)[^\\n]*?([\\w/\\.\\-]+\\.py)\")\n\n@dataclass\nclass Step:\n    action: str\n    args: dict = field(default_factory=dict)\n    ok: bool = True\n    stdout: str = \"\"\n    stderr: str = \"\"\n    tests_run: int = 0\n    tests_passed: int = 0\n    tests_failed: int = 0\n    new_failures: list = field(default_factory=list)\n    changed_files: list = field(default_factory=list)\n\ndef _touched(trace):\n    t = set()\n    for s in trace:\n        t |= set(s.changed_files or [])\n    return t\n\ndef classify_failure(trace):\n    ran = [s for s in trace if (s.tests_run or \"pytest\" in (s.stdout + s.stderr))]\n    if not ran:\n        return {\"label\": \"incomplete_verification\", \"confidence\": 0.5,\n                \"rationale\": \"no test run observed in the trace\"}\n    last = ran[-1]\n    if last.new_failures:\n        return {\"label\": \"regression\", \"confidence\": 0.8,\n                \"rationale\": f\"previously passing tests now fail: {last.new_failures[:3]}\"}\n    fail_files = set(_FAIL_LINE.findall(last.stdout + last.stderr))\n    touched = _touched(trace)\n    if last.tests_failed and fail_files and not (fail_files & touched):\n        return {\"label\": \"localization_error\", \"confidence\": 0.6,\n                \"rationale\": f\"failing tests {sorted(fail_files)[:2]} were never edited\"}\n    if last.tests_failed:\n        return {\"label\": \"implementation_error\", \"confidence\": 0.7,\n                \"rationale\": f\"{last.tests_failed} test(s) still fail after editing\"}\n    if last.tests_failed == 0 and last.tests_run:\n        return {\"label\": \"incomplete_verification\", \"confidence\": 0.3,\n                \"rationale\": \"observed tests pass; confirm the issue's own scenario\"}\n    return {\"label\": \"unknown\", \"confidence\": 0.2, \"rationale\": \"insufficient signal\"}\n\ndef next_action_for(trace):\n    c = classify_failure(trace)\n    c[\"next_action\"] = NEXT_ACTION[c[\"label\"]]\n    return c\n'''\n\nMODULES['budget.py'] = r'''\"\"\"Contribution C: budget-aware action selection by expected information gain.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nCOST = {\"search_similar_code\": 1.0, \"get_code_neighbors\": 1.0, \"get_code_subgraph\": 1.5}\nSTOP_THRESHOLD = 0.05\n\ndef _components_bonus(action, comps):\n    if action != \"get_code_subgraph\" or comps < 2:\n        return 0.0\n    return min(1.0, (comps - 1) / 2.0)\n\ndef score_action(cand):\n    action = cand.get(\"action\", \"\")\n    cost = COST.get(action, 2.0)\n    novelty = float(cand.get(\"novelty\", 0.0))\n    relevance = float(cand.get(\"relevance\", 0.0))\n    centrality = float(cand.get(\"centrality\", 0.0))\n    comps = float(cand.get(\"components\", 0.0))\n    if novelty <= 0.0:\n        return 0.0\n    gain = novelty * (0.6 * relevance + 0.4 * centrality)\n    gain += 0.3 * _components_bonus(action, comps)\n    return gain / cost\n\ndef score_actions(state):\n    scored = [{**c, \"score\": round(score_action(c), 4)} for c in state.get(\"candidates\", [])]\n    scored.sort(key=lambda c: c[\"score\"], reverse=True)\n    return scored\n\ndef decide(state):\n    ranked = score_actions(state)\n    if not ranked or ranked[0][\"score\"] < STOP_THRESHOLD:\n        return {\"stop\": True, \"reason\": \"marginal gain below threshold\", \"ranked\": ranked}\n    best = ranked[0]\n    return {\"stop\": False, \"action\": best[\"action\"], \"args\": best[\"args\"],\n            \"score\": best[\"score\"], \"ranked\": ranked}\n'''\n\nMODULES['env.py'] = r'''\"\"\"Navigation environment v2 (measures Contribution C without an LLM) with a FAIR cost model.\n\nv1 problems: every call to the 'lexical' policy used the graph-propagated ranking (prop_w=1.0 by default), and\nget_code_subgraph revealed an unbounded number of units, so policies were compared at different context costs.\nHere every action reveals at most k new units, 'rank' is the plain ranking read k at a time, and all policies use the\nsame base scores for relevance.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport random\nfrom . import budget\n\n\nclass NavEnv:\n    def __init__(self, loc, scores, order, gold, budget_calls=12, k=5):\n        self.loc, self.sc, self.order = loc, scores, order\n        hi = max(scores.values(), default=0.0) or 1.0\n        self.n = {u: s / hi for u, s in scores.items()}\n        self.gold, self.budget, self.k = set(gold or []), budget_calls, k\n        self.maxdeg = max([len(v) for v in loc.adj.values()] + [1])\n        self.visited, self.seq, self.calls, self.first_hit, self.expanded = set(), [], 0, None, set()\n\n    def unseen_top(self):\n        return [u for u in self.order if u not in self.visited][:self.k]\n\n    def nbrs(self, node):\n        nb = [m for m in self.loc.neighbors(node) if m not in self.visited and m in self.n]\n        return sorted(nb, key=lambda m: (-self.n[m], m))[:self.k]\n\n    def pooled(self):\n        pool = set()\n        for v in self.visited:\n            pool |= {m for m in self.loc.neighbors(v) if m not in self.visited and m in self.n}\n        return sorted(pool, key=lambda m: (-self.n[m], m))[:self.k]\n\n    def act(self, action, node=None):\n        self.calls += 1\n        if action == \"search_similar_code\":\n            new = self.unseen_top()\n        elif action == \"get_code_neighbors\":\n            new = self.nbrs(node)\n            self.expanded.add(node)\n        else:\n            new = self.pooled()\n        for u in new:\n            self.visited.add(u)\n            self.seq.append(u)\n        if self.first_hit is None and (self.gold & self.visited):\n            self.first_hit = self.calls\n        return new\n\n    def done(self):\n        return self.calls >= self.budget or bool(self.gold & self.visited)\n\n    def result(self):\n        return {\"hit\": int(bool(self.gold & self.visited)), \"first_hit\": self.first_hit, \"calls\": self.calls,\n                \"shown\": len(self.visited)}\n\n\ndef pol_rank(env, rng=None):\n    return (\"search_similar_code\", None)\n\n\ndef pol_random(env, rng):\n    if not env.visited:\n        return (\"search_similar_code\", None)\n    return (\"get_code_neighbors\", rng.choice(sorted(env.visited)))\n\n\ndef pol_graph_bfs(env, rng=None):\n    if not env.visited:\n        return (\"search_similar_code\", None)\n    best, bn = None, 0\n    for n in sorted(env.visited):\n        c = sum(1 for m in env.loc.neighbors(n) if m not in env.visited and m in env.n)\n        if c > bn:\n            best, bn = n, c\n    return (\"get_code_neighbors\", best) if best else (\"search_similar_code\", None)\n\n\ndef pol_best_first(env, rng=None):\n    \"\"\"Greedy: expand the highest-scoring visited node that still has unseen neighbours, else read more ranking.\"\"\"\n    if not env.visited:\n        return (\"search_similar_code\", None)\n    for n in sorted(env.visited, key=lambda x: (-env.n.get(x, 0.0), x)):\n        if n not in env.expanded and env.nbrs(n):\n            return (\"get_code_neighbors\", n)\n    return (\"search_similar_code\", None)\n\n\ndef _infogain(env, use_centrality):\n    if not env.visited:\n        return (\"search_similar_code\", None)\n    cands = []\n    top = env.unseen_top()\n    if top:\n        cands.append({\"action\": \"search_similar_code\", \"node\": None, \"novelty\": 1.0,\n                      \"relevance\": max(env.n[u] for u in top),\n                      \"centrality\": (sum(env.loc.degree(u) for u in top) / len(top) / env.maxdeg) if use_centrality else 0.0})\n    bn, bg, bu = None, -1.0, []\n    for n in sorted(env.visited):\n        unv = env.nbrs(n)\n        if unv and max(env.n[m] for m in unv) > bg:\n            bn, bg, bu = n, max(env.n[m] for m in unv), unv\n    if bn is not None:\n        cands.append({\"action\": \"get_code_neighbors\", \"node\": bn, \"novelty\": min(1.0, len(bu) / env.k), \"relevance\": bg,\n                      \"centrality\": (env.loc.degree(bn) / env.maxdeg) if use_centrality else 0.0})\n    pool = env.pooled()\n    if len(env.visited) >= 2 and pool:\n        cands.append({\"action\": \"get_code_subgraph\", \"node\": None, \"novelty\": min(1.0, len(pool) / env.k),\n                      \"relevance\": max(env.n[m] for m in pool), \"centrality\": 0.5 if use_centrality else 0.0,\n                      \"components\": 2})\n    d = budget.decide({\"candidates\": [{**c, \"args\": {}} for c in cands]})\n    if d.get(\"stop\"):\n        return (\"search_similar_code\", None)\n    pick = next(c for c in cands if c[\"action\"] == d[\"action\"])\n    return (pick[\"action\"], pick[\"node\"])\n\n\ndef pol_infogain(env, rng=None):\n    return _infogain(env, True)\n\n\ndef pol_infogain_nocent(env, rng=None):\n    return _infogain(env, False)\n\n\nPOLICIES = {\"rank\": pol_rank, \"random_walk\": pol_random, \"graph_bfs\": pol_graph_bfs, \"best_first\": pol_best_first,\n            \"infogain\": pol_infogain, \"infogain_no_centrality\": pol_infogain_nocent}\n\n\ndef run_nav(env, policy, seed=0):\n    rng, pol = random.Random(seed), POLICIES[policy]\n    while not env.done():\n        action, node = pol(env, rng)\n        env.act(action, node)\n    return env.result()\n'''\n\nfor name, text in MODULES.items():\n    (PKG / name).write_text(text)\nprint('wrote forgex v2:', sorted(MODULES))","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-17T01:43:49.751783Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-17T01:43:49.752021Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-17T01:43:49.773263Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-17T01:43:49.752001Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-17T01:43:49.772787Z"},"trusted":true},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"wrote forgex v2: ['__init__.py', 'ast_index.py', 'bm25.py', 'budget.py', 'env.py', 'failure.py', 'gold.py', 'graphprop.py', 'localize.py', 'metrics.py', 'similarity.py', 'tokens.py']\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":4},{"id":"941f98c5","cell_type":"code","source":"sys.path.insert(0, \"/tmp/forgex_pkg\")\nimport importlib, forgex\nimportlib.reload(forgex)\nfrom forgex import (index_repo, EvidenceLocalizer, parse_changes, gold_units, gold_files, rank_metrics, mean_rows,\n                    boot_ci, signflip_p, holm, paired, failure, budget, NavEnv, run_nav, POLICIES)\nimport tempfile, textwrap as _tw, difflib\n\n# ---- synthetic repo with a class, a free function, a duplicated name in two files, and a test file ----\n_d = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp()); (_d / \"pkg\").mkdir(); (_d / \"tests\").mkdir()\n_core = _tw.dedent(\"\"\"\n    class Base:\n        def run(self, x):\n            y = self.step(x)\n            return y\n\n        def step(self, x):\n            return x\n\n    def helper(a):\n        return a\n\"\"\")\n(_d / \"pkg/core.py\").write_text(_core)\n(_d / \"pkg/other.py\").write_text(\"def helper(a):\\n    return a 