from the harness: label the failed trajectories of the agent runs by hand and compare the classifier's labels against yours (see `forge_x_experiments.ipynb`, section 9).","metadata":{}},{"id":"b2da8258","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 7. Figures","metadata":{}},{"id":"b6f169b7","cell_type":"code","source":"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9.5, 4.2))\nnames = list(SYSROWS)\nmrr = [forgex.mean_rows(SYSROWS[n], [\"unit/mrr\"])[\"unit/mrr\"] for n in names]\ncis = [boot_ci([r[\"unit/mrr\"] for r in SYSROWS[n] if \"unit/mrr\" in r]) for n in names]\nax.bar(range(len(names)), mrr, yerr=[[m - c[0] for m, c in zip(mrr, cis)], [c[1] - m for m, c in zip(mrr, cis)]], capsize=3)\nax.set_xticks(range(len(names))); ax.set_xticklabels([n.split(\" \")[0] if n[0] == \"A\" else \"graph\" for n in names])\nax.set_ylabel(\"unit MRR (95% bootstrap CI)\"); ax.set_title(\"Contribution A: each step adds one thing\")\nfig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(CFG[\"OUT\"] / \"localization_chain.png\", dpi=140); plt.show()\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 4))\nfor K in CFG[\"GRAPH_KS\"]:\n    s = sens[sens.K == K]\n    ax.plot(s.beta, s[\"unit/mrr\"], marker=\"o\", label=f\"K={K}\")\nax.axhline(base[\"unit/mrr\"], color=\"gray\", ls=\"--\", label=\"no graph\")\nax.set_xlabel(\"graph weight beta\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"unit MRR\"); ax.legend(); ax.set_title(\"Graph weight: helps a little, hurts when large\")\nfig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(CFG[\"OUT\"] / \"graph_sensitivity.png\", dpi=140); plt.show()\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7.5, 4))\nax.bar(range(len(pols)), [nav_df.loc[p, \"hit@12 calls\"] for p in pols]); ax.set_xticks(range(len(pols)))\nax.set_xticklabels(pols, rotation=30, ha=\"right\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"hit@12 calls\"); ax.set_ylim(0, 1)\nax.set_title(\"Contribution C: no policy beats reading the ranking\")\nfig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(CFG[\"OUT\"] / \"navigation.png\", dpi=140); plt.show()","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-17T01:49:27.333129Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-17T01:49:27.33333Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-17T01:49:29.170408Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-17T01:49:27.333312Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-17T01:49:29.169799Z"},"trusted":true},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 950x420 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 700x400 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 750x400 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":11},{"id":"1ab015a7","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 8. Save results and build the corrected submission\nOnly measured values are written. The submission is a **single agent with the harness's built-in tools plus the analyzer sub-agent**: nothing in this notebook shows that the information-gain navigator, the failure classifier or an adapter improves anything, so none of them is shipped. The prompt tells the agent to use symbol names with `search_similar_code` (the README says the tool is symbol-oriented) and to keep scratch files in `/tmp`.\n\nWhat this notebook measured is *offline localization quality*. It does not predict the agent's pass rate; measure that with `swegemma eval` (see `forge_x_experiments.ipynb`).","metadata":{}},{"id":"bb4165cc","cell_type":"code","source":"manifest = dict(project=\"FORGE-X v2\", competition=\"gemma-4-developer-agent\", model=CFG[\"MODEL_ID\"], n_tasks=len(RES), seed=SEED,\n                repos=repos, systems=list(ALL_SYS), graph_choice_by_heldout_repo=picks,\n                versions=dict(python=platform.python_version()),\n                config={k: (str(v) if isinstance(v, Path) else v) for k, v in CFG.items()},\n                timestamp=time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"))\n(CFG[\"OUT\"] / \"run_manifest.json\").write_text(json.dumps(manifest, indent=1, default=str))\nprint(\"saved:\", sorted(p.name for p in CFG[\"OUT\"].iterdir()))","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-17T01:49:29.171963Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-17T01:49:29.17217Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-17T01:49:29.177727Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-17T01:49:29.172152Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-17T01:49:29.177253Z"},"trusted":true},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"saved: ['graph_sensitivity.csv', 'graph_sensitivity.png', 'localization_chain.png', 'localization_deltas.csv', 'localization_table.csv', 'navigation.png', 'navigation_deltas.csv', 'navigation_table.csv', 'phase1_rows.pkl', 'run_manifest.json']\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":12},{"id":"e4a4ca20","cell_type":"code","source":"MODEL = CFG[\"MODEL_ID\"]; B = CFG[\"SUB_BUDGET\"]\nGRAPH_TOOLS = [\"get_code_neighbors\", \"search_similar_code\", \"get_code_subgraph\"]\nBASE_TOOLS = [\"run_command\", \"read_file\", \"edit_file\", \"write_file\", \"get_status\", \"submit_patch\"]\n\nSYSTEM_MD = \"\"\"You are an expert autonomous software engineer fixing an issue in the repository at /workspace.\n\n## Goal\nMake the smallest correct change to SOURCE code so the behaviour described in the issue is fixed. A hidden test suite checks your patch.\n\n## How to work\n1. Localize first. Use identifiers from the issue (backticked names, classes, functions) as queries: call `search_similar_code` with a symbol name such as `Class.method` (it takes symbol names, not sentences), then `get_code_neighbors` on the best match to see callers and callees. You may delegate localization to the code_analyzer tool, which returns a short report.\n2. Read narrowly: use read_file with line ranges around the symbol you need.\n3. Edit in small steps: one logical change per edit_file call. Never paste whole files.\n4. Verify cheaply: run only the test file(s) that cover the code you changed (for example `pytest tests/test_x.py -k name -x -q`). Never run the whole suite. If an existing test fails for reasons unrelated to your change, ignore it.\n5. Keep scratch scripts in /tmp, not in /workspace. Never edit tests, conftest.py, pytest.ini, pyproject.toml, tox.ini or setup.cfg (those changes are discarded).\n5b. Budget: call get_status after every 4th tool call. When tool_calls_remaining is 5 or less, stop exploring, make your best edit, and submit.\n6. Finish: check that `git status` shows only intended source changes, call submit_patch (it is free), then give a one-line summary.\n\n## Rules\n- Follow exact error messages, exception types, status codes and signatures stated in the issue.\n- Do not refactor or reformat unrelated code.\n- Never end without a non-empty source patch.\n\"\"\"\nANALYZER_MD = \"\"\"You are a read-only code analysis sub-agent. Find where the reported issue lives; do not edit anything.\n\n1. Take identifiers from the issue (class, function, argument and message names) and locate them: call `search_similar_code` with a symbol name such as `Class.method`, then `get_code_neighbors` on the best match to see callers and callees.\n2. Read only the lines you need (read_file allows 150 lines per call).\n3. Reply in at most 150 words, no code blocks: file:line to change, the root cause in one or two sentences, and the smallest change that fixes it.\n\"\"\"\nSUB = CFG[\"SUBMISSION_DIR\"]\nshutil.rmtree(SUB, ignore_errors=True)\nfor d in (\"prompts\", \"configs\", \"sub_agents\"):\n    (SUB / d).mkdir(parents=True)\n(SUB / \"prompts/system.md\").write_text(SYSTEM_MD)\n(SUB / \"prompts/analyzer.md\").write_text(ANALYZER_MD)\n(SUB / \"configs/sampling.yaml\").write_text(\"temperature: 0.2\\ntop_p: 0.95\\nmax_output_tokens: 16384\\nthinking_config:\\n  include_thoughts: true\\n  thinking_budget: 4096\\n\")\n(SUB / \"eval_config.yaml\").write_text(f\"evaluation:\\n  timeout_seconds: {B['cmd_timeout']}\\n  max_tool_calls: {B['calls']}\\n  max_time_minutes: {B['minutes']}\\n  max_turns: {B['turns']}\\n\")\n(SUB / \"sub_agents/code_analyzer.yaml\").write_text(\n    f\"name: code_analyzer_agent\\ndescription: Analyzes repository source files and symbol graphs to locate root causes.\\nmodel: {MODEL}\\n\"\n    \"instruction: !include ../prompts/analyzer.md\\ntools:\\n\" + \"\".join(f\"  - {t}\\n\" for t in [\"read_file\"] + GRAPH_TOOLS) +\n    \"generate_content_config: !include ../configs/sampling.yaml\\n\")\n(SUB / \"agent.yaml\").write_text(\n    f\"name: forgex_v2\\nmodel: {MODEL}\\ninstruction: !include prompts/system.md\\ntools:\\n\" + \"\".join(f\"  - {t}\\n\" for t in BASE_TOOLS + GRAPH_TOOLS) +\n    \"  - agent_tool:\\n      config_path: sub_agents/code_analyzer.yaml\\n      skip_summarization: true\\n\"\n    \"generate_content_config: !include configs/sampling.yaml\\n\")\n\n# ---- offline structural validation (rules from HARNESS_README.md; not a substitute for the official validator) ----\nALLOWED_EXT = {\".yaml\", \".yml\", \".md\", \".txt\", \".py\", \".json\", \".safetensors\"}\ndef validate_submission(d):\n    d, errs = Path(d).resolve(), []\n    roots = [p for p in (\"agent.yaml\", \"agent.yml\", \"root_agent.yaml\", \"root_agent.yml\") if (d / p).exists()]\n    if len(roots) != 1:\n        errs.append(f\"need exactly one root config, found {roots}\")\n    models, adapters = set(), set()\n    for p in d.rglob(\"*\"):\n        if p.is_symlink():\n            errs.append(f\"symlink: {p}\")\n        if p.is_file() and p.suffix.lower() not in ALLOWED_EXT:\n            errs.append(f\"extension not allowed: {p.name}\")\n    for y in list(d.rglob(\"*.yaml\")):\n        txt = y.read_text()\n        models |= {m.group(1).split(\"/\")[-1] for m in re.finditer(r\"^\\s*model:\\s*(\\S+)\", txt, re.M)}\n        adapters |= {m.group(1) for m in re.finditer(r\"^\\s*adapter:\\s*(\\S+)\", txt, re.M)}\n        for m in re.finditer(r\"!include\\s+(\\S+)\", txt):\n            tgt = (y.parent / m.group(1)).resolve()\n            if d not in tgt.parents or not tgt.exists():\n                errs.append(f\"{y.name}: bad include {m.group(1)}\")\n        for m in re.finditer(r\"config_path:\\s*(\\S+)\", txt):\n            if not (d / m.group(1)).exists():\n                errs.append(f\"{y.name}: config_path missing {m.group(1)}\")\n    if models != {MODEL}:\n        errs.append(f\"expected exactly one base model {MODEL}, found {sorted(models)}\")\n    for a in adapters:\n        if not ((d / \"adapters\" / a / \"adapter_config.json\").exists() and (d / \"adapters\" / a / \"adapter_model.safetensors\").exists()):\n            errs.append(f\"adapter '{a}' is referenced but its folder is incomplete\")\n    return errs\n\nerrs = validate_submission(SUB)\nprint(\"validation:\", \"OK\" if not errs else errs)\nif not errs:\n    zp = shutil.make_archive(str(SUB.parent / \"submission\"), \"zip\", root_dir=SUB)\n    print(\"submission:\", zp, f\"({Path(zp).stat().st_size / 1e3:.1f} KB)\")\n    print(sorted(str(p.relative_to(SUB)) for p in SUB.rglob(\"*\") if p.is_file()))","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-17T01:49:29.178422Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-17T01:49:29.178619Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-17T01:49:29.206553Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-17T01:49:29.178602Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-17T01:49:29.206071Z"},"trusted":true},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"validation: OK\nsubmission: /kaggle/working/submission.zip (2.9 KB)\n['agent.yaml', 'configs/sampling.yaml', 'eval_config.yaml', 'prompts/analyzer.md', 'prompts/system.md', 'sub_agents/code_analyzer.yaml']\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":13},{"id":"f30d519c","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 9. Next steps\n1. **Measure pass rate, not localization.** Run the agent variants through the real harness (`forge_x_experiments.ipynb`): smoke test first, then the screening subset.\n2. **Treat the graph result as a hypothesis.** It is a small, uncorrected gain on 129 tasks from 4 repositories (one has a single task). A fresh repository would be the real test.\n3. **Do not ship components the data does